/-!
# Zelmanov Restricted Burnside
Category: Frontier — Fields Medal Work
Target: Frontier.zelmanov_restricted_burnside
Verification: pending
Provenance: Aristotle theorem prover (Harmonic)
-/

namespace Frontier

/-- `RestrictedBurnside m n` is the statement of the *restricted Burnside problem* for
`m` generators and exponent `n`: there is a uniform bound `N` on the order of every finite
group that is generated by `m` elements and has exponent dividing `n`.

(Equivalently, there are only finitely many isomorphism classes of such groups.)
Zelmanov's theorem asserts that `RestrictedBurnside m n` holds for all `m` and all `n ≥ 1`. -/

def RestrictedBurnsideClassTwo (m n : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Fintype G] (g : Fin m → G),
    Subgroup.closure (Set.range g) = ⊤ → (∀ x : G, x ^ n = 1) →
    commutator G ≤ Subgroup.center G → Fintype.card G ≤ N

/-! ## The abelian case -/

/-- An abelian group of exponent dividing `n > 0` generated by a finite family indexed by `ι`
has order at most `n ^ #ι`. -/
